<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Drama/Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Containment, Description, and a narrative inter spliced with exploration logs and journal entries</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Life came from the cold, dark crushing depths of the sea, and that is where it is most safe, supposedly</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Talassaphobia is the fear of deep ocean, and is super common, but at the same time the ocean is considered to be the origin of all life. This SCP is a cavern, with an entrance located in challenger deep, with multiple snaking tunnels to other locations the Foundation haven’t yet explored. It holds two main anomalous properties. Firstly: Low Hume levels, akin to the ‘Red Reality’ making it incredibly difficult for organisms to die via conventional means. Secondly: micro-organisms rapidly evolve or bond to new forms of life, ie: if a person enters this cavern with an exposed cute, micro-organisms will bind to it to heal said cut, or if left alone long enough, they will come together to form prehistoric-esque aquatic life. This main concept is linked to the start of life at the bottom of the sea, and these tunnels lead to ‘new earths’ giving life a start there. The main narrative centers around isolation, seeing as it is considered harder to reach the bottom of the sea then the moon. The research crew here are isolated for long stretches of time, and having a bare-bones facility, they begin to use the properties of this SCP to heal themselves, after one member takes a nasty injury. This is fine at first, but as they keep doing it, to themselves, and D-class provided to them, they start to become less than human. They start finding small mutations, healing with crustacean like plates over small cuts, and barnacle like acne on their skin. Eventually, between Foundation check ins, a total breakdown occurs: where the crew throws themselves into the SCP, and disappear into the tunnels, leaving only one comatose crewmate, recovered by the Foundation. The twist at the very end being that while the O5’s consider this “unfortunate” they have no plans to overhaul the site overlooking the SCP, inferring similar incidents will occur in the future.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> This SCP takes a common fear and twists it into something strangely safe, if a little twisted. If you're familiar with the abyss from <em>Dark Souls</em> its similar: more of the pitch black being the true, calm nature of life and less so the rampaging monsters. It explores isolation, survival, and twisting the notion of what the deep ocean and the beginning of all life is like.</p>

